 {"id":"QA-LORE-2","title":"[P2] QA upgrade cell graded a FOREIGN package: 'lore' name is squatted on PyPI by instacart/lore, so pip install lore==0.1.0 can never reach this project and any future publish under the name 'lore' is impossible","status":"pending","priority":"P2","phase":null,"created_at":"2026-09-27T06:10:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T06:10:00Z","complexity":2,"detail":{"fingerprint":"qa-battery-2026-09-27-bunker-las-02-agent-da3c20a6-upgrade-cell-lore-pypi-name-collision"},"reasoning":"Commands run (2026-09-27 QA battery, fresh JIT agent da3c20a6 on bunker-las-02): upgrade cell ran `pip install lore==0.1.0` on the clean agent -> rc=1, build wheel dies `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'app'` from lore/__init__.py line 1 (`from app import App`). Reproduced independently on the dev box in a fresh venv: identical rc=1 and identical traceback. Root cause verified from the artifact: `pip download lore==0.1.0` fetches lore-0.1.0.tar.gz whose PKG-INFO says `Summary: a framework for building and using data science / Home-page: http://github.com/instacart/lore / Author: Montana Low <montana@instacart.com>` and whose lore/__init__.py is `from app import App` -- the instacart/lore data-science framework, NOT this repo (our v0.1.0 tag tree has `from lore.classes import ...`, `__version__ = \"0.1.0\"` with no App import; verified via git show v0.1.0:lore/__init__.py). This project has never published to PyPI (RELEASE-LORE-001 confirms no release object), so the upgrade cell premise 'previous release installable from the registry' is false on any clean machine; the FAIL was a harness grading a stranger's sdist, not a product regression -- the cell itself should be UNVERIFIED (unpublished package), and QA-LORE-1 already tracks the missing tag/release making the path untestable. The PRODUCT finding filed here: the distribution name 'lore' is permanently occupied on PyPI by an unrelated 0.0-0.8.6 lineage, so (a) any `pip install lore` user gets instacart's package, never this one, and (b) a future publish under the current `name = \"lore\"` in pyproject.toml is impossible -- the project needs a distinct distribution name (e.g. lore-runbook / get-h3-lore) or a private index before RELEASE-LORE-001's cut, or the release surface will ship a name that cannot be installed. Fix direction: decide rename before cut; until then document in README/INSTALL that installs are from source (uv sync / pip install from the repo), never `pip install lore`."}
